## 2. Material Enactment Principle

### Principle ME

> A biological subject-bearing process is not an abstract causal topology instantiated by otherwise interchangeable matter. Its characteristic capacities depend partly on the specific causal powers of the material regime through which the organization is enacted.

Let:

[
\Sigma_i(t)
]

denote the material regime of process (A_i), including:

[
\Sigma_i=
\langle
W_i,I_i,L_i,P_i,C_i,E_i,M_i
